    <briefdescription>
<para>The fms module provides routines that are commonly used by most FMS modules. </para>    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para><simplesect kind="author"><para>Bruce Wyman</para></simplesect>
Here is a summary of the functions performed by routines in the fms module.</para><para><orderedlist>
<listitem><para>Output module version numbers to a common (<computeroutput>log</computeroutput>) file using a common format.<linebreak/>
</para></listitem><listitem><para>Open specific types of files common to many FMS modules. These include namelist files, restart files, and 32-bit IEEE data files. There also is a matching interface to close the files. If other file types are needed the <computeroutput>mpp_open</computeroutput> and <computeroutput>mpp_close</computeroutput> interfaces in module <ref refid="group__mpp__io__mod" kindref="compound">Mpp_io_mod</ref> must be used.<linebreak/>
</para></listitem><listitem><para>Read and write distributed data to simple native unformatted files. This type of file (called a restart file) is used to checkpoint model integrations for a subsequent restart of the run.<linebreak/>
</para></listitem><listitem><para>For convenience there are several routines published from the <ref refid="group__mpp" kindref="compound">MPP</ref> module. These are routines for getting processor numbers, commonly used I/O unit numbers, error handling, and timing sections of code. </para></listitem></orderedlist>
</para>    </detaileddescription>
  </compounddef>
